Package: gddlm
Title: Robust double linear models using gamma divergence
Version: 0.1
Date: 2025-07-01
Authors@R: c(
    person(c("Francis", "K.C."), "Hui", , "francis.hui@anu.edu.au", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0765-3533")),
    person("Shonosuke", "Sugusawa", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9495-4280"))
  )
Description: gddlm is designed to be a computationally fast (at least at
    the time of development!) method for robust double linear models based
    on the gamma divergence i.e., modeling the mean and (log of the)
    standard deviation in linear models assuming normally distributedd
    errors. The package works by applying the gamma divergence to the
    log-likelihood function of a double linear model to produce a new loss
    function (hence the name gddlm, which stands for gamma divergence
    double linear models) that is design to be produce inferences for the
    covariate effects on the mean and standard deviation that are robust
    to outliers.
